# Feedback Management

## 1. Introduction

The Feedback Management Module collects opinions and suggestions from students after they receive technical support. It helps measure the quality of the support service and identify areas for improvement.

## 2. Purpose

The main purposes of feedback management are:

* Measure student satisfaction
* Evaluate support quality
* Identify problems in the support process
* Collect suggestions
* Improve future support services

## 3. Feedback Process

The basic feedback process is:

```text
Student Receives Support
          ↓
    Problem Resolved
          ↓
    Feedback Form
          ↓
   Rating and Comments
          ↓
   Feedback Database
          ↓
   Support Improvement
```

## 4. Feedback Form

After a ticket is resolved, the student can provide:

* Rating
* Comment
* Problem resolution status
* Suggestions

### Example

```text
Ticket ID: T1001

Was your problem solved?
Yes

Support Rating:
5 / 5

Comment:
The support team provided a clear solution.
```

## 5. Rating System

A simple 1–5 rating system can be used.

| Rating | Meaning   |
| ------ | --------- |
| 1      | Very Poor |
| 2      | Poor      |
| 3      | Average   |
| 4      | Good      |
| 5      | Excellent |

## 6. Feedback Analysis

The administrator can analyze feedback to identify:

* Average rating
* Common complaints
* Frequently mentioned problems
* Support response quality
* Areas requiring improvement

## 7. Database Management

Feedback records can be stored with the following information:

| Field       | Purpose                       |
| ----------- | ----------------------------- |
| Feedback ID | Unique feedback number        |
| Ticket ID   | Related ticket                |
| Student ID  | Student who provided feedback |
| Rating      | Support rating                |
| Comment     | Student opinion               |
| Date        | Feedback date                 |

## 8. Benefits

Feedback management helps to:

* Improve support quality
* Understand student needs
* Identify weak areas
* Improve staff performance
* Measure user satisfaction
* Support continuous improvement

## 9. Feedback and Ticket Management

Feedback is connected to the ticket system.

```text
Student
   ↓
Create Ticket
   ↓
Support Staff
   ↓
Problem Resolved
   ↓
Ticket Closed
   ↓
Feedback
   ↓
Feedback Analysis
```

This allows feedback to be connected with the actual support request.

## 10. Privacy and Security

Feedback information should be protected from unauthorized access.

The system should provide:

* Secure login
* Controlled access
* Safe database storage
* Protection of student information

## 11. Future Improvements

Future versions can include:

* Automatic feedback reports
* Feedback dashboards
* Monthly satisfaction reports
* Support performance analysis
* Automatic identification of common complaints

## 12. Conclusion

The Feedback Management Module provides a simple way to understand student satisfaction and improve technical support. Regular analysis of feedback can help make the Virtual Customer Support System more reliable and user-friendly.
